 Description 
{{More citations needed section|date=March 2024}}
This herbaceous, tendril-bearing vine grows up to {{convert|5|m|abbr=on}} in length. It bears simple, alternate leaves {{convert|4–12|cm|abbr=on}} across, with three to seven deeply separated lobes. Each plant bears separate yellow male and female flowers. In the Northern Hemisphere, flowering occurs from June to July, and fruiting from September to November. It is a frost-tender annual in the temperate zone and a perennial in the tropics. It grows best in the USDA zones 9 to 11.

